<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Elemental Shaman DPS in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c7">Best in Slot Gear for Elemental Shaman DPS in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Elemental Shamans see a few major changes to itemization in Cataclysm: all DoTs can now crit, Mp5 is no longer a stat, as it was replaced by Spirit, which now doubles as Spell Hit rating through the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=30674/elemental-precision">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_elementalprecision_1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elemental Precision</span></a> talent. Most importantly, Cataclysm brings armor specialization - which means that wearing all mail grants us 5% extra Intellect through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86529/mail-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mail Specialization</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Overall, our primary gearing goals will be to stack Spirit /<wbr/> Hit until the 17% cap and then go for Haste, preferably obtaining enough to hit a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=8050/flame-shock">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_flameshock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flame Shock</span></a> breakpoint. Afterwards, Mastery and Crit both have their upsides and downsides, but Mastery is usually better, since <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=51505/lava-burst">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_lavaburst.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lava Burst</span></a> always crits already, regardless of your rating.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - This stat now gives Spell Power by itself, on top of the Mana and Crit that it provided in WotLK. We now gem Intellect, which is a red gem now, just like SP was.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit /<wbr/> Hit - The most efficient DPS stat until you hit the 17% Spell Hit cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste now affects our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=8050/flame-shock">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_flameshock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flame Shock</span></a> damage over time effect, as well as all spell casts like before. You will see extra effect from it when hitting Haste breakpoints for Flame Shock, but most of the benefit is from the cast time reductions.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - This is a new stat causes your spells to occasionally fire a duplicate spell for 75% damage and no threat. It has a good scaling with rating, making it a strong stat for DPS.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Crit is not strong for Elemental because of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=51505/lava-burst">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_lavaburst.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lava Burst</span></a> always critting, making extra crit have 0 value to increase its damage, and you also need a lot of crit rating to get 1% critical strike chance.</div></li></ol>
